spawn a, b, c
    a = 0:1 in table 0 row 0 {position velocity} at (1.0, 0.0)
    b = 1:1 in table 0 row 1 {position velocity} at (2.0, 0.0)
    c = 2:1 in table 0 row 2 {position velocity} at (3.0, 0.0)
despawn a: c is swapped into a's row, and its slot follows
    despawn returned ok
    a = 0:1 is dead
    c = 2:1 in table 0 row 0 {position velocity} at (3.0, 0.0)
spawn d: it reuses a's index with the next generation
    d = 0:2 in table 0 row 2 {position velocity} at (4.0, 0.0)
    a = 0:1 is dead
    a's position through the old handle is null
    despawning a again returns dead
    a zeroed handle 0:0 is dead
give b health: b moves to a new table and keeps its position
    b = 1:1 in table 1 row 0 {position velocity health} at (2.0, 0.0) health 75
    d = 0:2 in table 0 row 1 {position velocity} at (4.0, 0.0)
take b's velocity: another move
    b = 1:1 in table 2 row 0 {position health} at (2.0, 0.0) health 75
the tables, with the handles in each row
    table 0 {position velocity}: 2:1 0:2
    table 1 {position velocity health}:
    table 2 {position health}: 1:1
